  "data_start": "2024-12-01",
  "signal": "Each completed UTC daily close at the rolling highest close activates its independent long sleeve. Compare the close to the previously active trailing stop; otherwise raise it to max(previous stop, current channel midpoint). For a new long initialize the stop at that midpoint. If close is both a new high and through the old stop, give the high priority as in the published piecewise definition. Sleeve weight is active count/9. Size by a rolling 90-day sample standard deviation of simple close returns times sqrt(365), with scale capped at 2 per paper. Source25 targets 25% annual asset vol; Fixed50 targets 50%; Consensus targets 75% when at least six of nine sleeves are active and 25% otherwise. The last accepted scale is the reference for the 20% relative no-trade band on volatility-only changes. Signal state changes, monthly resets, and liquidity exits bypass the band.",
  "universe": "At 01:00 UTC on the first day of each month, rank the 36 existing Binance spot pairs by median quote turnover in the preceding calendar month. Eligibility requires 365 completed local days, and trailing 30-day median turnover >=2m USDT. Use top 20, alphabetical ties. Remove an asset through month end if trailing 30-day median daily quote volume drops below 1m or median absolute daily return drops below 0.5%. Maintain 1/20 target budget per name and keep unallocated weight as cash. Observe all signals after a one-hour delay. Reuse the historical state when a new cash book begins.",
  "adaptation": "Source25 is a local paper-derived control. Binance spot fixed survivor universe substitutes for the global CoinMarketCap panel. Single shared wallet with daily portfolio weights substitutes for independent monthly drifting sleeves. The relative no-trade band uses previously approved target scale; interpret the paper's price-change screen as absolute returns. Apply long-only cash cap and common 40% portfolio halt. Use the same method in both reset windows.",
  "execution": "Existing five-minute calendar replay, long/cash only, no funding, no leverage, max 20 names, aggregate target capped at 98%. Orders use the next completed five-minute close, adverse slippage of 3/10bps, and 10bps quote fee. Volume times candle low conservatively bounds quote turnover. Require 1% capacity; no certified lot/minimum-notional or order book. Start terminal exits at 23:00 UTC last day; sample NAV through midnight. Stops come from daily channel and account drawdown, not the replay's price stop set at zero.",
  "decision": "At both costs and in both windows Consensus must beat the positive return and return/drawdown of Source25 and Fixed50, hold positive return in both slices of the long window, have no halt and drawdown <=40%, and finish flat. Require >=25% annualized net in the long window at 20bps and >=20 complete lifecycles long/short windows. The recent short window is an unannualized gate. No live or paper admission without external evidence.",
